# BOHEMIA SIDE QUEST — PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# S06 — BEHIND THE FENCE  (the POST-WALL reveal / payoff)
# Reveal timing LOCKED 7/23 (Paolo): the daughter is NOT revealed during the pre-wall
# quests. Marco hides her, protects her; only AFTER the wall comes down does he trust
# you with the fact that she exists. "A sweet payoff and deep understanding type" beat.
# The title is now a double meaning — what was really behind the fence the whole time
# was her. This quest OPENS at that milestone (the wall coming down) and delivers the
# reveal, so it recontextualizes every guarded thing Marco did (see S09 THE BACK DOOR,
# the pre-wall boundary quest). Cast Marco against @ROLE neighbor; never named in a
# spoken line (W8). CLOUT is the mechanic's soul: receiving the trust quietly earns the
# DEEPEST bond and, deliberately, almost no followers (#quiet); turning his hidden child
# into public news earns MORE followers but breaks the trust he just gave you (#notable).

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# The corpus this quest is actually built from. Every id below resolves in
# records/BOHEMIA_QUESTBOOK_LAW_INDEX.json (3,672 citable findings mined out of
# the 152 studied quests in questbook/), and gates/quest_study_gate.js verifies
# the id AND the quoted law title verbatim. A citation is a claim the machine
# can check, never a name-drop.
# @STUDY Q112.P5  W9 (his biography arrives as extraneous info — our fold + [READ] + despair-with-a-thread-of-hope
#   applied: the daughter arrives as information you were not owed, and it recontextualizes every guarded thing he did.
# @STUDY Q001.W1  TRANSACTION-CARRIES-EMOTION
#   applied: the wall job is the errand; the trust is what actually changes hands.
# @STUDY Q001.W11  NO CLEAN WIN
#   applied: receiving the secret quietly earns the fewest followers and the deepest bond; cashing it earns the reverse.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_behind_fence   Behind the Fence
@ACT     1
@FACTION NONE
@ONCE    true

@ROLE neighbor  REQ  is=the_neighbor      household=behind_fence  wall_down=true
@ROLE daughter  REQ  is=neighbors_child   kept_hidden=true

@STAGE 10
  @LOG The wall between the two backyards is coming down today. Two grieving houses becoming one.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20
  @LOG The wall is down. He says there's something he couldn't tell me until it was.
  @DO show_objective 20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 30 COMPLETE #quiet
  @LOG He has a daughter. Kept hidden the whole time, until the wall and the trust were real. I held it quiet. The deepest bond, and nobody will ever know it happened.
  @DO bond neighbor +35
  @DO bond daughter +20
  @DO learn marco_has_a_daughter
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 31 COMPLETE #notable
  @LOG Told the compound there's a child here now. More eyes, more followers, and the one thing he protected is no longer his secret. He thanked me and didn't mean it.
  @DO bond neighbor -15
  @DO learn marco_has_a_daughter
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 32 FAIL #quiet
  @LOG Took the reveal badly, and he saw my face do it. He took it back. There's no daughter, he said. The wall might as well have stayed up.
  @DO bond neighbor -10

@OBJ 10  "Bring down the wall with the neighbor"   target=neighbor
@OBJ 20  "Hear what he could not say before"        target=daughter

@TALK wall  speaker=neighbor  entry=stage>=10
  @SAY Last brick. Look at that. Two yards, one yard. I didn't think I'd live long enough to knock this down. #hope
  @SAY There's a thing I have to tell you, and I couldn't tell you until this wall was on the ground. You'll understand why in about ten seconds.
  @OPT "Take your time."           [gate: none]  SILENCE -> reveal
  @OPT "Tell me."                  [gate: none]  -> reveal
  @NOVERB "Ask what he has been hiding"
@END

@TALK reveal  speaker=neighbor
  @SAY I have a daughter. #dread
  @SAY She's been inside the whole time. Behind that wall, in the back room, quiet as I could keep her. You don't tell people you have a child out here. Not until the wall is down and you're sure.
  @SAY Every time I came to your fence, every time I checked on you, I was measuring whether you were someone I could let her exist in front of. Today I decided you are. Don't make me wrong about that.
  @DO set_stage 20
  @OPT (say nothing, and let it be as big as it is)      [gate: none]  SILENCE -> grace
  @OPT "You've been protecting her this whole time."    [gate: none]  -> grace
  @OPT "There's a kid here now. People should know."      [gate: none]  -> loud
  @OPT (step back, thrown by it)                          [gate: none]  -> recoil
  @NOVERB "Promise nothing will ever happen to her"
@END

@TALK grace  speaker=daughter
  @SAY (a door opens behind him. she's small, and she doesn't come all the way out. she looks at you the way you look at weather you aren't sure of yet.)
  @SAY (her father doesn't say a word. he just watches the two of you deciding not to be afraid of each other, and something in his shoulders finally comes down, like a second wall.)
  @OPT (nod to her, and let her decide the rest)   [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 30
  @OPT "Hey. I'm just a neighbor. That's all."    [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 30
  @NOVERB "Promise nothing will ever happen to her"
@END

@TALK loud  speaker=neighbor
  @SAY No. No, you don't get to do that. #dread
  @SAY I told you. One person. I didn't tell the block, I didn't put it on the feed, I told the one person who earned the wall coming down. And you want to hand her to a crowd.
  @SAY It's done, they're looking now. Thank you for the wall. Go home. I need to go talk to my daughter.
  @OPT "I didn't think."          [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 31
  @OPT (leave, ashamed)            [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 31
@END

@TALK recoil  speaker=neighbor
  @SAY There it is. That's the face I was afraid of. #dread
  @SAY Forget I said it. There's no daughter. Help me stack these bricks back up, actually. On second thought, just go home.
  @OPT "Wait. I didn't mean it like that."   [gate: none]  -> reveal
  @OPT "Okay. I'm sorry."                     [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 32
@END
